Subject: [EXPERIMENT] Raise firmware TX retry ceilings to 15 attempts

The original policy sets both firmware retry ceilings from the default short
retry limit (7). Compare a ceiling of 15 while retaining the existing rate
policy, its termination flag, and mac80211 rate selection. This does not force
15 attempts for every frame: a shorter policy can terminate earlier.

This opt-in experiment trades additional radio attempts for fewer failed TX
confirmations. It is not an upstream fix or a promise of TLS deadlines.

--- a/tx.c
+++ b/tx.c
@@ -366,9 +366,9 @@
 			struct wsm_set_tx_rate_retry_policy_policy *dst =
 				&arg.tbl[arg.hdr.numTxRatePolicies];
 			dst->policyIndex = i;
-			dst->shortRetryCount = hw_priv->short_frame_max_tx_count-1;
+			dst->shortRetryCount = 14; /* experiment: 15 total attempts */
 			//only RTS need use longRetryCount, should be short_frame.
-			dst->longRetryCount = hw_priv->short_frame_max_tx_count-1;
+			dst->longRetryCount = 14;
 			
 			/* BIT(2) - Terminate retries when Tx rate retry policy
 			 *          finishes.
